Article 3
(1) Forms of violence, among others:
a. physical;
b. psychological;
c. sexual;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.
(2) The objectives of protection of Children and Women from acts of violence are:
a. to prevent and eliminate all forms of acts of violence and exploitation against children and women that occur in the family environment and society;
b. to seek recovery and social reintegration for children and women victims of violence;
c. to provide services to children and women victims of acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
d. to empower women victims of violence; and
e. to increase community participation.
(3) The implementation of protection of children and women from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (2), includes aspects of:
a. prevention;
b. services and assistance;
c. social reintegration; and
d. empowerment.
