Article 40
(1) In an effort to provide and organize the handling of services and protection for victims, the Regional Government and the Village Government establish the FPKK.
(2) The FPKK as referred to in paragraph (1) aims to:
   a. carry out efforts to prevent the occurrence of cases of violence;
   b. coordinate and synchronize the handling of PPT services;
   c. maintain and develop networks and referral systems; and
   d. collect, compile, and present reports on cases of violence.
(3) The management and membership of the Regency FPKK shall be determined by a Regent's Decree and the Village FPKK shall be determined by a Village Head (Lurah) Decree.
(4) The membership of the FPKK as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be grouped into the following roles:
   a. health role;
   b. psychology role;
   c. legal role;
   d. social role; and
   e. economic role.
(5) Further provisions regarding the establishment, main duties, and functions as well as membership of the FPKK as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by a Regent's Regulation.
